From 4b4a0738cf831e9e0318727031e1bd9eb4759e67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 09:22:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Line-by-line closing for duplicate-SKU order lines
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Warehouse report (GI-132076): an order listing the same SKU on two
lines (1 pc + 12 pcs) could never be packed cleanly — scans are
tallied per SKU, so every line displayed the SKU's full total (13/1
and 13/12), the pcs-left counter double-counted, and completion
compared each line against the same aggregate, making the order
impossible to complete.

Each line is now treated as a unique picking unit: the SKU's scan
total is allocated across its lines in file order (earlier lines fill
first, over-scan lands on the last line), so line 1 closes at 1/1,
line 2 at 12/12, independently. Applied consistently:

- scan table rendering, progress badge and pcs-left counter (client)
- per-row manual qty edits now edit that LINE's share
- completion mismatch check + completion slip export (server)
- scan feedback compares against the SKU's aggregate ordered qty,
  so counting reads "13/13 Complete" instead of a false OVER
- teach-barcode item list and carton slip aggregate per SKU instead
  of duplicating rows

Stored scan data is unchanged (still per-SKU totals) — no migration,
existing orders and exports keep working.

Verified in Chromium on a seeded 1+12 duplicate-SKU order: first scan
closes line 1 only, 13th closes line 2, progress reads 2/2 items, and
Complete succeeds with no mismatch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
